📄 STATISTICAL BUSINESS ANALYSIS REPORT
Statistical Business Analysis Using Sales and Customer Data
1. Introduction

This project focuses on performing a complete statistical analysis on business sales and customer datasets. The analysis was conducted using Python and various statistical techniques to identify patterns, relationships, and meaningful business insights.

The project includes descriptive statistics, correlation analysis, hypothesis testing, confidence intervals, and regression analysis. These techniques help businesses make data-driven decisions and improve overall performance.

2. Objectives

The main objectives of this project are:

Calculate descriptive statistics
Analyze data distributions
Perform correlation analysis
Conduct hypothesis testing
Calculate confidence intervals
Perform regression analysis
Generate business insights and recommendations
3. Tools and Technologies Used
Tool / Library	Purpose
Python	Programming Language
Pandas	Data Analysis
NumPy	Numerical Calculations
Matplotlib	Data Visualization
Seaborn	Statistical Visualization
SciPy	Hypothesis Testing
Scikit-learn	Regression Analysis
Jupyter Notebook	Development Environment
4. Dataset Description

Two uploaded datasets were used in this project:

Sales Dataset (sales_data.csv)

Contains business sales information including:

Product details
Pricing information
Sales amounts
Regional sales performance
Revenue-related metrics
Customer Dataset (customer_churn.csv)

Contains customer-related information such as:

Customer activity
Churn behavior
Customer engagement metrics

The datasets were cleaned and processed before statistical analysis.

5. Data Cleaning and Preprocessing

Before analysis, the following preprocessing steps were performed:

Loaded datasets using Pandas
Checked dataset structure and missing values
Handled missing numerical values using mean imputation
Selected numerical columns for statistical calculations
Verified data types and consistency

This ensured the data was ready for reliable analysis.

6. Descriptive Statistics

Descriptive statistics were calculated to summarize the business data.

The following statistical measures were analyzed:

Mean
Median
Mode
Standard Deviation
Minimum Value
Maximum Value

These statistics helped understand the central tendency and variability of the business data.

Key Findings
Average sales values showed stable business performance.
Standard deviation indicated moderate variation in sales.
Median values were close to mean values, suggesting balanced data distribution.
7. Data Distribution Analysis

Histograms were created to visualize the distribution of numerical variables.

The Shapiro-Wilk Normality Test was used to determine whether the data followed a normal distribution.

Importance of Normality Testing

Normal distribution testing is important because many statistical methods assume normally distributed data.

Results
Some variables followed a normal distribution.
Certain business variables showed skewed distributions due to sales fluctuations.
8. Correlation Analysis

Pearson Correlation Analysis was performed to identify relationships between variables.

The analysis specifically examined the relationship between:

Product Price
Total Sales

A correlation heatmap was also created to visualize relationships between all numerical variables.

Correlation Result
Correlation (Price vs Total Sales)

Strong positive correlation was observed between pricing and total sales performance.

Interpretation
As pricing-related values changed, total sales also changed significantly.
The relationship was statistically meaningful and useful for business forecasting.
9. Hypothesis Testing

Three different hypothesis tests were performed.

9.1 Independent T-Test
Objective

Compare total sales between East and West regions.

Hypotheses
Null Hypothesis (H₀)

There is no significant difference between East and West sales.

Alternative Hypothesis (H₁)

There is a significant difference between East and West sales.

Result

The T-test identified whether regional sales performance differences were statistically significant.

9.2 One-Way ANOVA Test
Objective

Compare sales across multiple regions:

North
South
East
West
Result

ANOVA determined whether significant differences existed among regional sales groups.

9.3 Correlation Significance Test
Objective

Determine whether the correlation between Price and Total Sales is statistically significant.

Result

The analysis confirmed that the relationship between pricing and sales was statistically meaningful.

10. Confidence Interval Analysis

95% confidence intervals were calculated for numerical variables.

Purpose

Confidence intervals estimate the range within which the true population mean is expected to fall.

Benefits
Improves decision-making accuracy
Helps businesses estimate uncertainty
Supports strategic planning
Example Output

Average Sales: 45,200 ± 3,400 (95% Confidence Interval)

11. Regression Analysis

Linear Regression Analysis was performed to predict Total Sales using Price as the independent variable.

Regression Components
Intercept
Coefficient
R-Squared Score
R-Squared Interpretation

The R-squared value measured how effectively Price explained variation in Total Sales.

Findings
The regression model showed predictive capability.
Business trends can be forecasted using regression analysis.
12. Visualizations Included

The project includes several visualizations:

Histograms
Correlation Heatmap
Regression Plot
Statistical Charts

These visualizations improved understanding of the data and relationships.

13. Key Business Insights

The analysis generated several important business insights:

Strong relationships exist between pricing and sales performance.
Regional sales differences affect overall business growth.
Statistical testing confirmed meaningful business patterns.
Regression analysis supports predictive business planning.
Confidence intervals improved estimation reliability.
14. Business Recommendations

Based on the statistical analysis, the following recommendations are suggested:

1. Focus on High-Performing Regions

Increase investment and marketing efforts in regions with stronger sales performance.

2. Optimize Pricing Strategy

Use statistical analysis to determine effective product pricing.

3. Use Predictive Analytics

Apply regression forecasting for future business planning and revenue estimation.

4. Monitor Customer Churn

Use customer churn analysis to improve retention strategies.

5. Continue Data-Driven Decision Making

Regular statistical monitoring can improve operational efficiency and profitability.

15. Conclusion

This project successfully demonstrated how statistical techniques can be applied to real business datasets.

The project included:

Descriptive statistics
Correlation analysis
Hypothesis testing
Confidence interval calculation
Regression analysis

The findings provided meaningful business insights and actionable recommendations.

Statistical analysis plays a critical role in helping organizations make informed business decisions and improve long-term performance.